----------
module local/test/m
----------

fun bump(mut x: int)
  set x = x + 1
end fun

----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

require module local/test/m

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

import m.bump

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

call bump(mut b)

----------
scriptunit-fragment 5
----------

let c = b * 2

----------
scriptunit-fragment 6
----------

let d = 100

----------
expect all six units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 126 |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 3 | reads `m` (2) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 4 | reads `bump` (3), updates `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 5 | reads `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 252 |
| 6 | - | compiles, runs | new | `d` = 100 |

----------
module-edit local/test/m
----------

fun bump(mut x: int)
  set x = x * 2
end fun

----------
expect the body of `bump` is edited
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 4 reruns and updates `b`, so `b` has to be as unit 4 first found it | `b` = 250 |
| 2 | - | untouched | it only requires the module, which still compiles | - |
| 3 | reads `m` (2) | reruns | imports from the module | - |
| 4 | reads `bump` (3), updates `b` (1) | reruns | reads `bump` | - |
| 5 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 4 | `c` = 500 |
| 6 | - | untouched | uses nothing | `d` = 100 |

----------
module-edit local/test/m
----------

fun bump(ref x: int): int
  ret x + 1
end fun

----------
expect `bump` stops writing its argument
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 4 updated `b` when it last ran, and no longer compiles | `b` = 125 |
| 2 | - | untouched | it only requires the module, which still compiles | - |
| 3 | reads `m` (2) | recompiles, runs | imports `bump`, whose signature changed | - |
| 4 | - | recompile fails | `bump` no longer takes `mut` | - |
| 5 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b`, which unit 4 no longer updates | `c` = 250 |
| 6 | - | untouched | uses nothing | `d` = 100 |

----------
module-edit local/test/m
----------

fun bump(mut x: int)
  set x = "nope"
end fun

----------
expect the module stops compiling
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | nothing changed `b` | `b` = 125 |
| 2 | - | recompile fails | requires a module that does not compile | - |
| 3 | - | recompile fails | imports from a module that does not compile | - |
| 4 | - | recompile fails | `bump` is gone | - |
| 5 | reads `b` (1) | untouched | nothing changed `b` | `c` = 250 |
| 6 | - | untouched | uses nothing | `d` = 100 |

----------
engine
----------

| unit | this step | note |
|------|-----------|------|
| 1 | recompiles | the module leaving the compile changes what every unit is typechecked against |
| 5 | recompiles | the module leaving the compile changes what every unit is typechecked against |
| 6 | recompiles | the module leaving the compile changes what every unit is typechecked against |

----------
module-edit local/test/m
----------

fun bump(mut x: int)
  set x = x + 10
end fun

----------
expect the module is fixed
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | `b` is as unit 1 made it | `b` = 135 |
| 2 | - | reruns | requires the module, which compiles again | - |
| 3 | reads `m` (2) | recompiles, runs | imports from the module, which compiles again | - |
| 4 | reads `bump` (3), updates `b` (1) | recompiles, runs | `bump` is back | - |
| 5 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 4, which updates it again | `c` = 270 |
| 6 | - | untouched | uses nothing | `d` = 100 |

